<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34765" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percussĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				beating</i>, <i>striking</i> (class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capitis percussiones,</span>”
				<i>beatings on the head</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 3, 26, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">digitorum,</span>”
				<i>a snapping</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Off. 3, 19, 75</span></i>
			.  —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in music and rhetoric, <i>a beating time;</i> hence, concr., <i>time</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percussiones numerorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 47, 182</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percussionum modi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Or. 58, 198</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 3, 108
		al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
